; A match whose arms are all literals, with nothing to catch the
; rest. Exhaustiveness only ran when the scrutinee's type named a
; declared `data`, so this checked OK - and when no arm matched at
; run time, control fell through to the merge block and the match
; answered its freshly allocated result cell's contents: 0, at exit
; 0, indistinguishable from a real answer. docs/memory-model.md
; MM-VAL-9b; refused since 2026-08-14. (A bool match carrying BOTH
; `true` and `false` arms still checks - it cannot fall through.)
(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (match 7 ((1) 11) ((2) 22)))
